  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To subtract $-1.5$ from $8$, we combine the two negative signs to make a single plus sign. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8-(-1.5)=8+1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate $8+1.5$, we start at $8$ and move $1$ place to the right. Then, we move another $0.5$ places to the right: \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14150464/assets/6c5594e76467d574192f48b23ef994e9d86afbff76f3fb75c34082445e938774.png)\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n8-(-1.5)=9.5.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
